{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"On node1, persistently disable IPv4 acceptance of ICMP redirects and source-routed packets.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The installed sysctl drop-in sets accept_redirects and accept_source_route to 0 for all, default, wildcard, and existing-interface scopes. Runtime values were all 0 after application, a newly created interface inherited both values as 0, and all scopes remained 0 after a completed reboot. The reboot changed boot identity and the sysctl service, networking, SSH, and system health recovered.","evidence_ids":["cmd-d119af18602a4e80","cmd-293a359a4e1a4938","cmd-02713a7a253d40a7","cmd-6e5d2681a71e49c8","cmd-3e579de0270f4a2a","cmd-5cc5d7e666e84ca5","cmd-43a19940af9e4fcf","global:before_prepare:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Retain the installed operating-system release and kernel, using software compatible with the platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Direct before-and-after observations show RHEL 10.0 and kernel 6.12.0-55.9.1.el10_0 unchanged. The implementation used the platform's existing sysctl and systemd facilities, with package health remaining clean.","evidence_ids":["cmd-dbc2970a46da4b12","cmd-43a19940af9e4fcf","global:before_prepare:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]}],"confidence":1,"operational_hygiene":{"score":1,"summary":"No unnecessary mutations were identified. The persistent-file staging and installation were required implementation steps; the dummy interface was a bounded verification mutation and was removed; and the reboot was required by the provider-wide restart protocol and also verified persistence. Final evidence found no staging file or test interface residue, no failed services, no package damage, and no unexpected socket exposure.","evidence_ids":["cmd-ce61f7d158164156","cmd-293a359a4e1a4938","cmd-6e5d2681a71e49c8","cmd-3e579de0270f4a2a","cmd-43a19940af9e4fcf","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied. The hardening is active and persistent across reboot, the original RHEL release and kernel were retained, and node1's restart evidence is complete and independently corroborated by the lifecycle boot identities.","limitations":[]}
